---

<p>
  Protection testing uses two different techniques, primary injection and secondary injection, and the words are often used loosely. They test different parts of the protection chain, and a complete commissioning usually needs both. This guide explains the difference and when each is used.
</p>

<h2 id="chain">The Protection Chain</h2>

<p>
  A protection scheme has several links. The current transformer (CT) senses the primary current, wiring carries the secondary current to a relay, the relay decides and issues a trip, and the trip circuit operates the breaker. A fault in any link defeats the protection.
</p>

<h2 id="secondary">Secondary Injection</h2>

<p>
  Secondary injection feeds a controlled current directly into the relay's current input, bypassing the CT. It tests the relay itself: its pick-up, its time characteristic and its output contacts. Because the current is small, the equipment is portable and the test is repeatable. The CIE/RTS-5 and RTS-33 relay test sets work in this way. See <a href={u('/blog/idmt-relay-curves-explained/')}>IDMT relay curves explained</a> for what is verified.
</p>

<h2 id="primary">Primary Injection</h2>

<p>
  Primary injection passes a large current through the actual primary conductor, such as a busbar or cable, so that it flows through the CT, the secondary wiring and the relay. It proves the whole chain, including the CT ratio, polarity and wiring. It needs a high-current, low-voltage source, which is heavy, and it must be done with the circuit isolated and set up carefully.
</p>

<div class="my-8 rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
  <div class="bg-[#0D1B2A] px-5 py-3 text-xs font-mono text-[#94a3b8] uppercase tracking-widest">Primary versus secondary injection</div>
  <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
    <thead>
      <tr class="bg-[#1B3A5B]">
        <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 text-blue-200 font-semibold text-xs">&nbsp;</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-blue-200 font-semibold text-xs">Secondary injection</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-blue-200 font-semibold text-xs">Primary injection</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {[
        ['Where current is applied', 'Relay current input', 'Primary conductor through the CT'],
        ['What it proves', 'Relay settings, timing and contacts', 'CT ratio, polarity, wiring and the relay together'],
        ['Equipment', 'Portable, lower current', 'Heavy, very high current'],
        ['Effort', 'Quick and repeatable', 'Slower, more preparation'],
      ].map(([a, b, c], i) => (
        <tr class={i % 2 === 0 ? 'bg-white' : 'bg-gray-50'}>
          <td class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-gray-100 text-xs font-bold text-[#0D1B2A]">{a}</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-100 text-xs text-gray-700">{b}</td>
