        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<Callout type="warning" title="CT secondaries must never be open-circuited">
  An energised CT with an open secondary can develop a dangerously high voltage. Always short the CT secondary before working on wiring, and follow the isolation and shorting procedure for the scheme.
</Callout>

<h2 id="which">Which Do You Need?</h2>

<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 my-4">
  <li>Routine maintenance on an existing relay: secondary injection is usually enough.</li>
  <li>New installation or replaced CT or wiring: primary injection is normally added to prove the whole path.</li>
  <li>Fault investigation: start with secondary to rule out the relay, then primary if the cause is not found.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="what-cie">What CIE Supplies</h2>

<p>
  CIE's relay test sets are secondary injection instruments, and we do not supply primary injection sets. They cover single-phase over-current and earth fault testing and three-phase testing with phase angle control for directional and distance relays. See <a href={u('/products/relay-test-sets/')}>relay test sets</a>, and read <a href={u('/blog/how-to-choose-a-relay-test-set/')}>how to choose a relay test set</a> and <a href={u('/blog/substation-pre-commissioning-tests-checklist/')}>the substation pre-commissioning checklist</a>.
</p>

